<title>YEMEN: Yemen approves oil deal with Hungary's MOL.</title>
<headline>Yemen approves oil deal with Hungary's MOL.</headline>
<dateline>SANAA 1997-07-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Yemen's cabinet on Tuesday gave its final approval for an oil production sharing agreement signed in April with Hungary's oil and gas company MOL, state radio reported.</p>
<p>The company's concession is in sector 49 of Sabwa governorate, east of the capital Sanaa.</p>
<p>Yemeni state television reported earlier that under the terms of the deal the company would carry out seismic surveys and drill exploratory wells in the area in two phases. The work will cost at least $8 million.</p>
</text>
